        "comments": "The assembly fAcaLat1.1 is based on 60x Illumina genome survey data, 106x Illumina Hi-C data, 282x PacBio data, and 100x Illumina transcriptome data generated at Nextomics Biosciences. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Falcon-unzip, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, Hi-C based scaffolding with SALSA2, Arrow polishing, and two rounds of FreeBayes polishing. Finally, the assembly was analysed and manually improved using gEVAL. Chromosome-scale scaffolds are named by synteny to the GCA_900880675.1 assembly of Sparus aurata.",
